(footprint "Keepout_Rear_MainsPour" (version 20221018) (generator hwflow_parts) (layer "F.Cu")
  (descr "No copper pour on any layer over the rear-board mains zone (R8): a GND pour must stay 6 mm (creepage) from AC_* copper and may not lie under mains traces. Tracks, vias and pads stay allowed: AC_* copper lives here. The polygon points are BOARD coordinates of the 130 x 40 mm panel (KiCad stores the zones of a footprint in board coordinates). The rear board is drawn mirrored in the panel region x 0-62 (panel x = 62 - board x), so the zone is panel x 0-55.7, y 13-40 (board x 6.3-62). Notches to y 12 at panel x 4.6-13.6 and 36.5-45.5: the relay NC pads 12 (K2 at x 9.1, K1 at x 41.0, y 19.6, r 1.2) are live in the reset state; the pour edge at y 13 gave 5.4 mm creepage (KiCad DRC), at y 12 it gives 6.4 mm.")
  (tags "keepout mains pour")
  (attr exclude_from_pos_files exclude_from_bom)
